# Daily operation logging — discussion and first build requirement

Date: 2026-10-30. Author: Codex Prime.
State: bounded addition to the next Prime-cycle pass; no automatic chat export.

Director words from this conversation:
"Yes, I think we need to start building logging into what is actually happening on a daily basis now. We have been avoiding it but et will need to become part of the process."

The next cycle pass should log the commands actually invoked, input/registration
identities, outputs and exits, refusal/partial states and resulting review identities.
Prime's reasons and semantic choices remain on the work-local review record. The
journal references that source rather than becoming another editable decision ledger.
Machine-observed events and Prime-entered context must be distinguishable.

Keep a practical first scope: instrument only this tool's own read, record, inspect
and packet entry points, including failed attempts. Do not claim to capture every
chat turn, shell command, external model action or Director instruction automatically.
Incoming conversation capture/attachment remains a separate unbuilt connection.

Daily summaries should show attempts, failures/holds, finished passes, completed
goals and unknown/incomplete operations using their actual source records. A replay
is another invocation, not a second completion. Missing time/usage remains unknown.
Dates/times need explicit basis; do not use a template's old date as execution time.

A failed logger must not hide a committed review or turn a partial operation into
success. Use a caller-declared bounded journal destination, preserve incomplete
attempts, and document recovery. Keep the existing work records authoritative.

First factual log below is manual Prime review context plus the wrapper-observed
capture verification event. It is not evidence that an automatic daily logger exists.
